    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155-a2">

                <pb facs="0265" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg259"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">M. du Chaylard to the Chamber of Commerce.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulat de France à Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                25, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    submitted to my colleagues the letter which you addressed to me under date of
                    February 13 last, relative to the proposed measures in connection with the river
                    improvement scheme. The consular body will do all in their power to further the
                    measures which the Chamber of Commerce proposes, and will, as soon as they
                    receive it, carefully go into the scheme which you promise to submit.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Du Chaylard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
